# Featured service staff picker (s3.1.19)

Resume: `@featured-staff$` / `$staff-picker$`.

Owner decision (Oct 7 2026): **keep the featured-staff logic as originally programmed** — `clubLocations/{id}.featuredStaff` is a hand-curated list and `club-profile-app.js` `renderPeople` shows exactly that list. Only the **input** changed. Do not auto-publish the roster, and do not add `isDisplayedOnClubPage` / `displayGroup` datapoints unless the owner asks again.

## UI (`admin.html` → Club Public Profile → card `.featured-staff-card`)

- `#featuredStaffPicker` replaces the old `#clubProfileFeaturedStaff` textarea. DJs and promotion groups keep their textareas.
- One row per person: checkbox, avatar, name and club roles. When ticked: **Role on the club page** input (prefilled) and a photo strip.
- Photo strip = the person's own pictures (`photoURL`, `profilePhotoUrl`, `publicPhotoUrl`, `avatarUrl`, image `profileMediaSlots`), https only, plus **Upload from computer** (JPG/PNG/WebP/GIF ≤ 10 MB) → Storage `clubMedia/{locationId}/featuredStaff/{ts}-{file}` (public read, signed-in write). No URL fields.
- Changes are a draft (`featuredStaffDraft` Map keyed `uid:{uid}` or `name:{normalized}`) until **Save Public Profile**, which writes `featuredStaff: FLOQRFeaturedStaff.toFeatured(featuredStaffRows())`.

## Logic (`floqr-featured-staff.js`, `window.FLOQRFeaturedStaff` + `module.exports`)

`buildRows({roster, featured, rolesOf})`: saved entries first (ticked, original order, matched to roster by uid then by normalized name), then remaining roster people (unticked, role = first non-“Club Admin” role). Roster = `clubRoster()` (Employee Network: linked to this club with a role). Entries not on the roster stay listed as “Added by hand”; unticking and saving removes them.

`toFeatured(rows)`: ticked rows → `{...original, name, role, photoUrl, uid?, photoStoragePath?}`; extra fields of existing entries (`bio`, `instagram`, `publicProfileType`…) are preserved; empty fields dropped. Shape stays compatible with `club-profile-app.js` and the AI index.

Render runs after both `loadClubPublicProfile` (clears the draft) and `loadEmployeeDesignations`, so whichever finishes last fills the list.

## Photo consent (s3.1.20)

Owner (Oct 7 2026): keep the workflow; add a notice that admins must have the employee's consent before publishing **photos** (names/roles do not need it). Legal stance: club is the controller; FLOQR records the attestation, it does not collect the employee's own consent.

- Amber `.featured-staff-consent` box under the picker: notice + checkbox `#featuredStaffPhotoConsent` + record line `#featuredStaffConsentRecord`.
- `photoSignature(featured)` = sorted `keyFor(entry)|photoUrl` lines for entries with a photo. `needsPhotoConsent(featured, stored)` = signature non-empty and ≠ `stored.photoSignature`.
- Save (`featuredStaffConsentPayload`): no photos → nothing; stored consent still matches → keep it; otherwise the box must be ticked for the current signature or save throws `featuredStaff.consentRequired` **before** the `clubLocations` write. Writes `featuredStaffPhotoConsent {photoSignature, photoCount, confirmedByUid, confirmedByEmail, confirmedAtIso}`.
- Adding or changing any photo changes the signature → box unticks → fresh attestation required.
- Website feed (`design-notes-club-website-feed.mdc`) publishes staff photos only when the stored signature matches; otherwise names/roles only. `club-profile-app.js` (FLOQR page) is unchanged.

## Caveats

- Picking a staff profile picture stores its Storage download URL (token URL, works signed-out). If the person deletes that picture, the club card falls back to their initial. Uploads from the computer live under the club and are not affected.
- `firestore.rules` `users` is readable by signed-in users (open finding in `design-notes-feature-services.mdc`); the picker reads the same `users` list the Employee Network already loads.

Tests: `functions/featured-staff-picker.test.js`. i18n: chrome `featuredStaff.*` (20 keys × 11 packs, incl. 5 consent keys), help `help-featured-staff` (venueAdmin).
